**Before:** Read `parsedData.location` and `parsedData.quantity_kg` via loose `(parsedData as any).x` casts (defensive, since the old schema's shape wasn't fully trusted). No use of `quality`, `urgency_level`, or `impact_tags` — those fields didn't exist yet.

**After:**
- Imports the real `ParsedSMSData` type instead of relying on `any` casts — `parsedData.location`, `parsedData.quantity_kg`, `parsedData.urgency_level` are now typed and safe to read directly.
